  "turns": [
    {
      "input": "Hadrik Voss gives Nicco a pair of leather boots.",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Hadrik Voss tugs the leather boots from where they'd been hanging at his belt, examining them briefly with the same scrutiny he gives cracked mail—checking seams, flexing the leather at the ankle, finding them sound enough if not remarkable. He extends them toward Nicco without ceremony, his magnifying lenses still perched on his nose from whatever he'd been working on before arriving in the square. \"These came through. Nothing wrong with them. Take them if they fit.\"\n\nThe boots hang in the space between them, offered but not forced, and the dwarf's attention already seems half on whatever task had occupied him before—his broad shoulders angled slightly back toward the tower's entrance or the street beyond. Hadrik Voss does not eye Nicco's own footwear or make any observation about what he wears; the transaction, such as it is, stands complete once Nicco either accepts or declines.",
